Build with the Xcode 16 iig: add IORPC.kernelContent (as in xnu-11215).

GitHub Actions retired the macos-14 runner images (2026-11-02), so the
kernel is now built on macos-15 where only Xcode 16.x / 26.x are available.
The Xcode 16+ iig generates IORPC dispatchers (_Dispatch stubs in the
*.iig.cpp files compiled into the kernel) that read the message back via
    message = rpc.kernelContent;
instead of calling IORPCMessageFromMach(rpc.message, false) like the
Xcode 15 iig did.  The `IORPCMessage *kernelContent` member of struct
IORPC was only added in macOS 15 (xnu-11215), so xnu-8796 does not have
it and the generated code fails to compile.

Backport the field (guarded by #ifdef KERNEL, exactly as Apple does in
xnu-11215) into both copies of IORPC.h, and populate it at every point
in IOUserServer.cpp where an IORPC reaches an iig-generated dispatcher:
OSMetaClassBase::Invoke(), IOUserServer::kernelDispatch(), the rpc
initializer in IOUserServer::server() and IOUserServerUEXTTrap().

This is the inverse of blacktop/darwin-xnu-build patches/14.4+15.0
iokit.patch, which rewrites `message = rpc.kernelContent` back to
IORPCMessageFromMach() to build NEW xnu with an OLD iig.
diff --git a/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h b/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
--- a/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
+++ b/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
@@ -224,6 +224,9 @@
 	IORPCMessageMach * reply;
 	uint32_t           sendSize;
 	uint32_t           replySize;
+#ifdef KERNEL
+	IORPCMessage     * kernelContent;
+#endif /* KERNEL */
 };
 typedef struct IORPC IORPC;
 
diff --git a/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h b/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
--- a/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
+++ b/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
@@ -224,6 +224,9 @@
 	IORPCMessageMach * reply;
 	uint32_t           sendSize;
 	uint32_t           replySize;
+#ifdef KERNEL
+	IORPCMessage     * kernelContent;
+#endif /* KERNEL */
 };
 typedef struct IORPC IORPC;
 
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOUserServer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOUserServer.cpp
